## Why This Is Asked
Tests that cover client-side persistence and recovery from autosave are common in product forms. This checks basic E2E skills without server integration.

## Key Concepts
- E2E testing of client-side autosave via localStorage
- Time control with cy.clock and cy.tick
- Form state restoration after reload
- Cleanup of autosave after completion

## Code Example
```javascript
describe('Profile Wizard Autosave', () => {
  it('restores autosaved progress after reload', () => {
    cy.clock();
    cy.visit('/profile/new');
    cy.get('#firstName').type('Alex');
    cy.tick(120000);
    cy.window().then(win => {
      const data = JSON.parse(win.localStorage.getItem('profile_wizard'));
      expect(data?.firstName).to.eq('Alex');
    });
    cy.reload();
    cy.get('#firstName').should('have.value', 'Alex');
  });
});
```

